# DTF tier manifest: proxy-scan-record-only-provenance  (artifact-keeper
# 1.11.0: #3645 / #3868 record-only proxy scanning and its audit, #3013
# finding_class, #3014 vulnerability-DB provenance on scan results)
# Profile-set: filesystem + the mock-scan-formats upstream (Maven fixtures
# whose pom.properties name commons-text 1.9 and log4j-core 2.14.1).
# LOCAL-ONLY: verdicts and findings come from the backend image's bundled
# Grype and its pre-seeded DB; the malicious-package finding is ingested
# through POST /api/v1/security/findings/external (no OSV, no internet).
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS:
#   * #3645/#3868: proxy_scan_action=record_only scans and records every
#     proxied pull but never withholds one (X-AK-Scan: pending, then
#     recorded); hyphenated spellings are 400; a Virtual that enforces wins
#     over a record-only member; every scan-config change is audited as
#     REPOSITORY_UPDATED with before/after and the changed field names.
#   * #3013: findings carry finding_class; the findings list filters on it
#     (closed vocabulary, typo 400); a MAL-* id is classed malicious and
#     graded critical whatever severity the scanner reported.
#   * #3014: scan results report vuln_db_version / vuln_db_published_at
#     (grype-db-v<schema> for Grype, live:osv for the dependency scanner).
#
# Red: ak-backend:1.10.0. Green: ak-backend:1.11.0 and newer.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-scan-formats"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
